    <location value="14"/>
    (which was not certified by peer review) is the author/funder. All rights reserved. No reuse allowed without permission. bioRxiv preprint doi: https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.07.08.737248; this version posted July 12, 2026. The copyright holder for this preprint
  </page_header>
  <text>
    <location value="35"/>
    <location value="48"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="431"/>
    comprehensive virtual cell would predict how a genetic perturbation reshapes the transcriptome, 1 classify cell identity from a gene-expression profile, reconstruct tissue architecture from spatially 2 resolved measurements, and explain its predictions in biologically interpretable language. 3 Realizing this vision would compress decades of accumulated biological knowledge into an 4 executable form, with high application value for in silico perturbation screening, cell-type atlas 5 construction, spatial pathology, and clinical decision support. 6 Recent advances in foundation models have brought this vision closer to reality. Transformer7 based architectures pretrained on tens of millions of cellular profiles -scGPT (Cui et al., 2024), 8 Geneformer (Theodoris et al., 2023), scFoundation (Hao et al., 2024), UCE (Rosen et al., 2023), 9 and CellPLM (Wen et al., 2024) -yield transferable representations of gene programs and cell 10 states. For spatial transcriptomics, SToFM, Nicheformer (2025), and HEIST (2025) extend 11 representation learning to tissue context but require dedicated spatial-aware architectures; 12 concurrent work applying language models directly to single-cell or spatial data includes CeLLM 13 (Li et al., 2024), ST-LLM (Wang et al., 2024), Cell2Sentence (C2S, Ou et al., 2024), C2S-Scale 14 (Yang et al., 2024), and AlphaCell (2025), which we discuss in turn below. In perturbation 15 prediction, GEARS (Roohani et al., 2024) established graph neural networks over Gene 16 Ontology as the academic benchmark, achieving Pearson correlation 0.84 on the Norman 2019 17 dataset. 18 Despite this rapid progress, three classes of specialized foundation models have emerged, each 19 advancing one capability but none addressing all. These limitations collectively prevent any 20 existing foundation model from serving as a true virtual cell. 21
  </text>
