    UMAP visualization of pancreas embeddings (16,382 cells, 14 cell types) is shown alongside five competing models in Figure 3a. The visual impression of cluster compactness is supported quantitatively by the normalized mutual information metric in Figure 2b: on the pancreas dataset OCellus achieves NMI = 0.71, substantially higher than scGPT (0.66), Geneformer (0.05), scFoundation (0.64), and PCA (0.65), and second only to scimilarity (0.74) which is specifically optimized for cell-type similarity search. NMI measures the agreement between clustering
  </text>
