    (which was not certified by peer review) is the author/funder. All rights reserved. No reuse allowed without permission. bioRxiv preprint doi: https://doi.org/10.64898/2026.07.08.737248; this version posted July 12, 2026. The copyright holder for this preprint
  </page_header>
  <text>
    <location value="35"/>
    <location value="48"/>
    <location value="449"/>
    <location value="386"/>
    For perturbation prediction, Pearson correlation is computed between predicted and true log2 1 fold-change values on the top twenty differentially expressed genes per perturbation, and 2 direction accuracy measures the fraction of genes whose predicted direction matches the true 3 direction. GEARS is reproduced using the official implementation with default hyperparameters 4 (hidden dimension 64, twenty epochs) on the Replogle 2022 dataset under our pseudo-bulk top5 20-DE evaluation protocol; literature values for scGPT (0.80) and CPA (0.78) are taken from 6 scPerturBench and may reflect a different evaluation protocol. The binary protein-protein7 interaction task uses positive pairs from STRING v12 at confidence ≥ 700 and negative pairs 8 sampled randomly from the same gene pool (degree-matched negatives are deferred to future 9 work). Cell-cell communication annotations on the spatial-cellchat task follow the conventions 10 of CellPhoneDB (Efremova et al., 2020), LIANA+ (Dimitrov et al., 2024), and NicheNet 11 (Browaeys et al., 2020); OCellus learns ligand-receptor relationships implicitly from training 12 data and does not query any external ligand-receptor database at inference time. 13 All confidence intervals are reported as 95 percent bootstrap intervals computed by resampling 14 test cells or perturbations with replacement (10,000 resamples for cell-type benchmarks; 2,000 15 for perturbation). The Wilson score interval is used for binary-classification rates such as the 16 OCellus-Agent pipeline accuracy. Ablation experiments use three random seeds (42, 123, 2024) 17 and report mean ±  standard deviation. We follow the TRIPOD-AI reporting guidelines (Collins 18 et al., 2024) for AI-based prediction models. 19
  </text>
